# Line endings: LF, everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set on the machines this is developed from, and it
# converts on checkout and inside `git archive`. Nothing in this repository
# wants CRLF, and two things break outright on it:
#
#   deploy/run-deploy.sh and deploy/tunnel.sh are scp'd to a Linux server and
#   run there. `set -euo pipefail\r` is not a shell option, and bash reports it
#   as "set: pipefail: invalid option name" from a file that looks correct in
#   every editor.
#
#   deploy/pary.service is read by systemd, where a trailing \r becomes part of
#   the value — ExecStart pointing at a binary whose name ends in ^M.
#
# The same thing cost a working day in the kElir repository before the rule was
# written down there, including five signing tests that failed because babel
# normalises a template literal to \n while fs.readFileSync keeps a fixture's
# \r\n, so indexOf could never match. Nothing in that test was wrong.
#
# One catch before trusting a check: `git archive <commit>` reads .gitattributes
# from the tree it is archiving, not from the working tree, so this has no
# effect on an archive of any commit made before it was committed. Pass
# --worktree-attributes to apply it anyway.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never converted, never diffed as text.
*.db      binary
*.vsix    binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.docx    binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
